      "question_or_instruction": "explain what is mean by emi",
      "answer": "You asked me to explain what EMI means. \n\nEMI stands for Equated Monthly Installment. It's the fixed amount you pay each month to repay a loan. In your case, the EMI is $313.36, which you need to pay on or before the 8th day of each month, starting from November 8, 2025. \n\nThis amount is calculated based on the loan amount, interest rate, and tenure of the loan. It's usually a fixed amount that remains the same throughout the loan period, unless you make any changes to the loan terms. \n\nIn your agreement, the EMI is applied first to any accrued interest and then to the principal balance. This means that you'll pay a portion of the interest and a portion of the loan amount each month.",
